CGRA Fmax trajectory  (board: nexys_a7 = Nexys 4 DDR, xc7a100tcsg324-1, speed -1)
================================================================================

Status after the 2026-09-19 audit: the numeric entries below are historical
claims, not validated measurements of the current RTL. Raw reports/checkpoints
must be archived and the corrected reset/step timing must be rerun in Vivado.
The old formula 1000/(period-WNS) and the claim that phys_opt only improves
results were invalid. Do not use those entries as certified Fmax values.

Current method: `make -f hw.mk fmax [STEP_DIV=N] [FLOORPLAN=1]` searches
candidate periods and validates a fresh final implementation with phys_opt.
Only if setup AND hold pass does it report 1000/period and append to
fmax_validated_history.csv. This is a checked candidate, not a proof of a
global maximum; changing constraints does not change the board oscillator.
One logical step takes STEP_DIV clocks; reset-to-first-step spacing is now
also checked by GHDL.
Constraint recap: the ALU datapath is an N-cycle multicycle path with N=STEP_DIV
(step fires every Nth clock). At period T the datapath has N*T while
control/reset/IO paths have T. Small N => the datapath sets the wall; large N =>
the single-cycle control paths do.

